|text=Bogs are acidic peatlands, characteristic of boreal forests and mountainous regions (Figures 9.3 and 9.4). Their hydrology is precipitation driven as bogs do not receive floodwaters from neighboring rivers and streams{{nb...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2019-02-19|author=Sincere Humphrey|title=Freshwater Microbiology|publisher=Scientific e-Resources|isbn=9781839473500|page=24
|text=Bogs are acidic peatlands, while fens are non-acidic peatlands. The thick mat of dead plants forms sphagnum moss and peat, which is where we get our peat moss. Over a long period of time, the bog may fill up and a forest will grow in{{nb...}}}}
